name 'aif-y2-working-with-data-preassessment-q15-2026'

wrong 'There is a strong relationship between the two variables.'
wrong 'There isn\'t a strong relationship between the two variables.'
right 'The more hours someone spends on their phone, the less time they spend reading books.'
wrong 'The more hours someone spends on their phone, the more time they spend reading books.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

markdown <<MARKDOWN
A survey asked people about how many hours they spend on their phone and how many hours they spend reading books. Which **best** describes the relationship the data shows between these two variables?

| Daily Hours on Phone | Daily Hours Reading Books |
|---|---|
| 5 | 1 |
| 4 | 1 |
| 4 | 2 |
| 3 | 3 | 
| 3 | 3 |
| 2 | 4 |
| 2 | 4 |
MARKDOWN

